The vendor's power drivers read the device-tree node of a power supply from its of_node field. Upstream removed that
field, since the same node is already in its dev.of_node ("power: supply: core: get rid of of_node", 134254038739),
and the 6.6 stable line took it in 6.6.163 as a dependency of "power: supply: core: Honor supplied-from with
CONFIG_OF=y". This reads dev.of_node instead, in the four drivers this config builds and in the two typec ones it
does not, so enabling those later does not break the build again.
todo: remove when the vendor tree is based on 6.6.163 or later and carries this itself.

--- a/bsp/drivers/power/supply/sunxi_usb_power.c
+++ b/bsp/drivers/power/supply/sunxi_usb_power.c
@@ -295,7 +295,7 @@
 
 	memset(&gpio_para, 0, sizeof(gpio_para));
 
-	gpio_para.gpio = of_get_named_gpio(psy->of_node, gpio_name, 0);
+	gpio_para.gpio = of_get_named_gpio(psy->dev.of_node, gpio_name, 0);
 	if (gpio_para.gpio < 0) {
 		PMIC_INFO("%s not detected\n", gpio_name);
 		return 0;
